{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>ויתנכר.</b> He said: if I reveal myself to them, they will say — you too are sworn and undertaking not to reveal us; or perhaps they will flee in fear of me, and my father will grieve. Better that they come through the distress of the famine, and I will press them to bring Binyamin, and I will detain him, and through this the matter will become known. [ויתנכר אליהם — it is a person's way, when he does not wish to do kindness with his relatives, to make himself as though he does not recognize them.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:22.319535547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}